{"name":"Batik Pink","hex":"#9c657e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"batik","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wax-resist method of dyeing fabric."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dye fabric using the wax-resist method."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/batik"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Batik","blocks":[{"text":"Batik is a dyeing technique using wax resist. The term is also used to describe patterned textiles created with that technique. Batik is made by drawing or stamping wax on a cloth to prevent colour absorption during the dyeing process. This creates a patterned negative when the wax is removed from the dyed cloth. Artisans may create intricate coloured patterns with multiple cycles of wax application and dyeing. Patterns and motifs vary widely even within countries. Some patterns hold symbolic significance and are used only in certain occasions, while others were created to satisfy market demand and fashion trends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Batik_Trusmi_Cirebon_%2823%29.jpg/330px-Batik_Trusmi_Cirebon_%2823%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batik","wikidata":"Q635427"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Niya_batik.jpg/250px-Niya_batik.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Niya_batik.jpg/500px-Niya_batik.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Niya_batik.jpg/250px-Niya_batik.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANiya_batik.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Egypt%2C_Byzantine_period%2C_1st_half_of_6th_century_-_Resist-Dyed_Hanging_with_Biblical_Scenes_-_1951.400_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-250px-Egypt%2C_Byzantine_period%2C_1st_half_of_6th_century_-_Resist-Dyed_Hanging_with_Biblical_Scenes_-_1951.400_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Egypt%2C_Byzantine_period%2C_1st_half_of_6th_century_-_Resist-Dyed_Hanging_with_Biblical_Scenes_-_1951.400_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Egypt%2C_Byzantine_period%2C_1st_half_of_6th_century_-_Resist-Dyed_Hanging_with_Biblical_Scenes_-_1951.400_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Egypt%2C_Byzantine_period%2C_1st_half_of_6th_century_-_Resist-Dyed_Hanging_with_Biblical_Scenes_-_1951.400_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-250px-Egypt%2C_Byzantine_period%2C_1st_half_of_6th_century_-_Resist-Dyed_Hanging_with_Biblical_Scenes_-_1951.400_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm